Kana quiz — licensing boundary
==============================

This repository separates application code from generated third-party data.

  Everything EXCEPT src/data/generated/   MIT                 — see LICENSE
  src/data/generated/                     Source-specific     — see
                                                                src/data/generated/LICENSE

Most generated data is adapted from CC BY-SA dictionaries, so ShareAlike reaches
it; CEJC and Tatoeba have the carve-outs recorded in the directory licence. The
data licences do not reach the code: the code reads the data, it is not derived from
it, so the two are distributed as a collection rather than combined into an
adaptation, and CC BY-SA 4.0 does not require a collection apart from the work
itself to be licensed under its terms.

The stroke-order data (src/data/generated/strokes/) is adapted from KanjiVG
(© Ulrich Apel and contributors, CC BY-SA 3.0). CC BY-SA 3.0 folds into this
CC BY-SA 4.0 collection as an allowed licence upgrade. Full attribution is in
src/data/generated/LICENSE.

vocab.json's `beginnerRank` field also incorporates two JLPT lists (tanos.co.uk,
CC BY; open-anki-jlpt-decks, MIT) and OpenSubtitles frequency (hermitdave/
FrequencyWords, CC BY-SA 4.0). CC BY and MIT are both compatible with being
folded into a CC BY-SA 4.0 work; OpenSubtitles is itself CC BY-SA 4.0. Full
attribution is in src/data/generated/LICENSE; the source snapshots live under
scripts/ingest/sources/.

cejc-reading-frequency.json is a reduced educational analysis of the National
Institute for Japanese Language and Linguistics' Corpus of Everyday Japanese
Conversation (CEJC), version 2022.09. It is not relicensed as CC BY-SA; its use
remains subject to CEJC's terms. The raw CEJC archive is not distributed. See
the CEJC carve-out in src/data/generated/LICENSE.

If you fork this: take the code under MIT and preserve the source-specific terms
and attribution recorded in src/data/generated/LICENSE for generated data,
including the CEJC and Tatoeba carve-outs.
